infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title CRUD vs event sourcing: what each write stores
  desc Same order #48291 — overwrite the latest snapshot, or append an immutable fact
  compares
    - label CRUD: UPDATE overwrites the row
      children
        - label Stores the latest snapshot only
          desc One row per order holds the current status; prior states are gone
        - label Each UPDATE destroys the prior state
          desc UPDATE orders SET status='approved' erases 'pending'
        - label Records the after-image — just the number 5
          desc No who, no why, no reason behind the change
        - label Audit rebuilt from logs: ~6 hours, partial
          desc History reverse-engineered from app logs and memory
    - label Event sourcing: append an immutable fact
      children
        - label Stores every business event, append-only
          desc Events are never updated, never deleted
        - label Current state is a left-fold of the log
          desc events.reduce(applyEvent, initialState) — derived, not stored
        - label Captures intent + context
          desc OrderApproved with approved_by and a reason code
        - label Temporal query is trivial: filter + fold
          desc Fold the prefix up to any past timestamp for exact state
theme
  palette #f43f5e #6366f1
